	doi = {10.1038/nrn3901},
	abstract = {The brain is a complex, interconnected network; the connection topology of the brain thus fundamentally shapes the onset, expression and progression of brain disease.To understand disorders of the brain requires knowledge of how brain networks respond — either adaptively or maladaptively — to pathological perturbation.The burgeoning field of connectomics is providing new tools for describing and modelling these responses.The effects of brain disease depend critically on the topological centrality and degeneracy of the affected regions; pathology of central regions exacerbates maladaptive responses, whereas degeneracy facilitates adaptive responses},
